  "excludedCandidate": "The earlier keyboard/device-center scroll risk was not exercised: failure precedes Book title tap and every text-input/hideKeyboard/scroll settings command.",
  "repairProposal": {
    "status": "Proposed to root; no source edit in this review",
    "scope": [
      "src/components/memory/MemoryFilm.tsx",
      "src/components/memory/MemoryMovieExport.tsx"
    ],
    "change": "Use explicit iOS dismissal completion: set Modal visible=false while retaining the mounted component; stop playback/cancel export and release resources immediately; invoke parent close/read/post handoff only from onDismiss. Android can finalize immediately because onDismiss is iOS-only. Fence duplicate close and late/unmounted handoffs.",
    "reason": "Both components currently render a visible Modal and are conditionally unmounted by their parent on close. Film-to-reader also updates the underlying book in the same commit. Retaining them until native dismissal completes avoids recycling modal/content views and beginning parent presentation work while UIKit is still dismissing.",
    "proofLimit": "The artifact establishes a real settings presentation failure, correct targeting, mounted settings content, and no keyboard involvement. It does not uniquely prove early recycling as the cause. Focused actual-component lifecycle regression plus the next required native run must validate a repair; do not relax selectors/timeouts."
  },
